  "notes": "Pattern B by definition -- there is no University Park major named 'Media and Communication' (checked Backend/degree_plans/ for every CAS/COMM-adjacent title; UP's closest analogues are separate majors like Communication Arts and Sciences, Journalism, etc., none of which share this exact name or course list). This is a genuine Behrend-only B.A. combining CAS (Communication Arts and Sciences) and COMM (Communications) coursework. Required major courses (45cr total, matching the bulletin's stated major-credit total exactly): Prescribed (16cr) -- CAS 204, CAS 212, CAS 303, COMM 160, COMM 251, COMM 260W; three alt-pairs (9cr) -- CAS 271N or COMM 205, CAS 450W or CAS 252, COMM 494 or COMM 495; electives within the major (5cr) -- one of COMM 242/270/282 (3cr) plus two picks from COMM 1/3/4 (1cr each, both real 1-credit special-topics-style courses per Backend/catalogs/comm_catalog.json); and 15cr of Supporting coursework (min. 9cr at 400-level, modeled as 2 generic + 3 explicitly-400-level slots since the bulletin doesn't enumerate a fixed Supporting course list -- an adviser-driven open pool, same convention used elsewhere in this repo for majors whose bulletin leaves a category unenumerated). COMM 260W's real prerequisite (COMM 160 done, plus ENGL 15/30H) is respected by scheduling COMM 160 in an earlier semester. General Education (45cr) and Bachelor of Arts Degree Requirements (24cr: World Language through Level 3 = 12cr, BA Knowledge Domain x3 = 9cr, World Cultures = 3cr) are modeled generically (not sub-divided into every individual PSU GenEd knowledge-domain bucket), consistent with this repo's existing convention for majors with open GenEd choices. This plan totals ~119.5cr, slightly under the bulletin's own stated 124cr total -- an honest approximation from the generic-slot modeling, not a missing-requirement error (every named, enumerable requirement from the bulletin's own required-course list is present).",
